    "result_text": "The build passes. The other two files in the test directory (`AcceptanceBase`, `AuditLogCapture`) are support classes, not test classes, so `AcceptanceTest` is the full runnable suite and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `customerCode` for a new owner is generated in `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`. I added de-duplication there, keeping each piece of logic in its proper place:\n\n- **`CustomerCodeGenerator`** stays a pure formatter \u2014 it produces the base `<REGION>-<HASH8>` code and has no need to know about existing owners.\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl`** owns the collision check, since it's the layer with repository access \u2014 consistent with its existing `countNamesakes` / `countHouseholdMembers` helpers that also query stored owners.\n\nThe new private helper `deduplicateCustomerCode`:\n1. Collects the set of non-null `customerCode`s already stored.\n2. Returns the code unchanged if it's free.\n3. Otherwise appends `-<n>`, scanning from `n = 2` upward for the smallest suffix that isn't taken, and returns that de-duplicated code.\n\n`saveOwner` now generates the base code, runs it through the helper, and stores the result \u2014 so downstream fields derived from `customerCode` (e.g. the membership number) use the de-duplicated value.",
